{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#518","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#518","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#518\",\"parent_revision\":\"9b57e27516fc463ec941b4bc5ce7766301f883ed115ea73cf5d2a45d14427f66\",\"root_revision\":\"9b57e27516fc463ec941b4bc5ce7766301f883ed115ea73cf5d2a45d14427f66\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe FM009 state machine in plugin_validator.py:_fix_unquoted_colons does not differentiate between scalar top-level lines (mcp: null) and block-introducer lines (mcp:). When a scalar line like `mcp: null` is encountered, current_top_level_key is set to 'mcp'. Any subsequent indented line (orphaned indent \u2014 impossible in valid YAML but possible in malformed frontmatter) is then incorrectly treated as inside the mcp: block and skipped by the ecosystem guard, leaving an unquoted colon unfixed and invalid YAML in production SKILL.md files. The fix requires detecting scalar vs block top-level lines and resetting current_top_level_key after a scalar so subsequent indented lines are not suppressed.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: FM009 orphaned-indent after scalar mcp: null suppresses colon fix\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Confirm whether the state-machine bug still exists in the current skilllint implementation and fix or close accordingly.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. _fix_unquoted_colons implementation location | AVAILABLE | skilllint is an external package; _fix_unquoted_colons at skilllint/plugin_validator.py:158 in the installed cache (1.8.0)\\n2. Current implementation approach | AVAILABLE | As of skilllint 1.8.0, _fix_unquoted_colons uses a flat regex (no current_top_level_key state machine) \u2014 the state machine approach described in the bug report appears to have been replaced\\n3. ecosystem_registry.py integration | AVAILABLE | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ecosystem_registry.py; tests in test_ecosystem_registry.py reference FM009 skipping logic\\n4. Test coverage for mcp: null + orphaned-indent edge case | DERIVABLE | requires writing a reproducing test against current skilllint version to determine if the regex approach has the same gap\\n5. Upstream fix target | DERIVABLE | skilllint is external; fix requires upstream PR or forked override in this repo\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 3\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nNote: The state machine described in the bug report (current_top_level_key) is NOT present in skilllint 1.8.0. Implementation was redesigned. Verification step required: confirm if the flat-regex implementation still exhibits the mcp: null suppression bug before implementing a fix.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED with verification gate \u2014 confirm bug still exists in 1.8.0 before committing to implementation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Write a reproducing test: SKILL.md frontmatter containing `mcp: null` on one line followed by an indented line with an unquoted colon is passed to `_fix_unquoted_colons`; verify whether the colon on the indented line is fixed or suppressed\\n- [ ] If bug confirmed: fix the flat-regex implementation in `skilllint` upstream (or fork/patch if upstream won't accept) so that lines following `mcp: null` are not incorrectly suppressed\\n- [ ] If bug NOT confirmed (flat-regex handles it correctly): close #518 with evidence comment linking to the test result\\n- [ ] `uvx skilllint@latest check --fix` on a SKILL.md with `mcp: null` and a subsequent line with an unquoted colon produces correct output\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_ecosystem_registry.py` and any new regression test pass\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `skilllint/plugin_validator.py` \u2014 external package; `_fix_unquoted_colons` at line 158 (installed cache: /root/.cache/uv/archive-v0/CpqG-9JW_rpFeEjRF05sb/lib/python3.11/site-packages/skilllint/plugin_validator.py)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ecosystem_registry.py` \u2014 FM009 skip logic\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_ecosystem_registry.py` \u2014 existing FM009 skip tests\\n- Any new reproduction test: `plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_fm009_mcp_null_regression.py`\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a **plugin developer running `uvx skilllint`**, I want **`_fix_unquoted_colons` to correctly handle `mcp: null` scalar top-level lines** so that **unquoted colons in lines immediately following a scalar `mcp: null` are not incorrectly suppressed by an ecosystem guard, leaving invalid YAML in production SKILL.md files**.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **fm009 orphaned-indent after scalar mcp: null suppresses colon fix** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | plan/P027-multi-ecosystem-plugin-creator-followup-3.yaml | current | dh_migrate | 2026-03-24T16:34:50Z |\\n| task-plan | plan/P028-multi-ecosystem-plugin-creator-followup-3.yaml | current | dh_migrate | 2026-03-24T16:34:53Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review \u2014 tasks-26 followup analysis (2026-03-06)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ecaeffa6bc8315957e2e58ad94bc294541dd01bb5a5e8d78beb2c14b16a762b5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTCwcQ\"}"}